# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the SonicBoom quality gate.
#
# Policy: suppress only allocations whose root is outside SonicBoom ownership
# (uninstrumented runtimes or their process-lifetime singletons). A leak rooted
# in core/, capi/, or a compiled graph must fail the gate.
#
# This file is intentionally empty until a measured, reproducible third-party
# singleton requires an entry. Add a suppression only with:
#   * the exact stack (from .quality/logs/<run>/sanitizers-lsan-ctest.log)
#   * why the allocation is process-lifetime / owned by an external runtime
#   * the date and the commit at which it was observed
